e":"print"},{"key":"19_33426970","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"81","DOI":"10.1016\/j.elspec.2004.09.029","volume":"143","year":"2005","journal-title":"J ELECTRON SPECTROSC RELAT PHENOM"},{"issue":"2-4","key":"20_18110063","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"73","DOI":"10.1016\/j.ultramic.2003.08.002","volume":"98","author":"Howie","year":"2004","journal-title":"Ultramicroscopy","ISSN":"http:\/\/id.crossref.org\/issn\/0304-3991","issn-type":"print"},{"key":"21_25883578","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"127","DOI":"10.1016\/0304-3991(91)90113-K","volume":"38","year":"1991","journal-title":"Ultramicroscopy","ISSN":"http:\/\/id.crossref.org\/issn\/0304-3991","issn-type":"print"},{"issue":"3-4","key":"22_17729489","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"453","DOI":"10.1016\/S0304-3991(03)00107-4","volume":"96","author":"Schattschneider","year":"2003","journal-title":"Ultramicroscopy","ISSN":"http:\/\/id.crossref.org\/issn\/0304-3991","issn-type":"print"}],"container-title":["Journal of Electron Microscopy"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/academic.oup.com\/jmicro\/article-pdf\/58\/3\/213\/5852634\/dfn027.pdf","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2019,2,17]],"date-time":"2019-02-17T00:56:46Z","timestamp":1550365006000},"score":56.78942,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/academic.oup.com\/jmicro\/article-lookup\/doi\/10.1093\/jmicro\/dfn027"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2009,1,13]]},"references-count":18,"journal-issue":{"issue":"3","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2009,5,18]]},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2009,6,1]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1093\/jmicro\/dfn027","ISSN":["0022-0744","1477-9986"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0022-0744","type":"print"},{"value":"1477-9986","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2009,1,13]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2023,1,19]],"date-time":"2023-01-19T14:54:04Z","timestamp":1674140044405},"reference-count":3,"publisher":"Cambridge University Press (CUP)","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2020,6,18]],"date-time":"2020-06-18T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1592438400000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":9818,"URL":"https:\/\/www.cambridge.org\/core\/terms"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Proc. annu. meet. Electron Microsc. Soc. Am."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1993,8,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Recently, a new method of interferometry has been realized which is capable of providing important information of crystals, crystal defects and electron-optical information of the microscope such as its spherical aberration surface. The method produces interferograms by using an electron biprism to interfere diffracted beams produced from a small convergent beam probe of \u223c10 nm. The electron biprism uses an applied voltage of \u223c15 to 100 V to deflect and compensate for the diffracted beam(s) of 2\u03b8<jats:sub>B<\/jats:sub> (typically \u223c5 mrad) (Fig. 1). The biprism \u223c0.3 \u03bcm dia) is inserted in between and perpendicular to the diffracted beam(s). Two biprism positions were successfully used. An \u201cupper\u201d biprism is placed in the selected area aperture position which is between the objective lens and 1st intermediate lens. A \u201clower\u201d biprism is further down the optic axis and is placed between the 1st and 2nd intermediate lenses. In Fig. 1, the virtual image of a biprism is shown with respect to the specimen plane.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1017\/s0424820100151118","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2020,6,18]],"date-time":"2020-06-18T09:53:16Z","timestamp":1592473996000},"page":"1056-1057","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["Convergent beam electron diffraction interferometry using an electron biprism (CBED+EBI)"],"prefix":"10.1017","volume":"51","author":[{"given":"R.A.","family":"Herring","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"G.","family":"Pozzi","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"T.","family":"Tanji","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"A.","family":"Tonomura","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"56","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2020,6,18]]},"reference":[{"key":"S0424820100151118_bib03","unstructured":"3) Herring, R. A. and Tanji, T. , these MSA proceedings."},{"key":"S0424820100151118_bib01","unstructured":"1) Herring, R. A. , Pozzi, G. Tanji, T. , and Tonomura, A. , Ultramicroscopy, Accepted for publication."},{"key":"S0424820100151118_bib02","first-page":"77","volume":"65","author":"Pozzi","year":"1983","journal-title":"Optik"}],"container-title":["Proceedings, annual meeting, Electron Microscopy Society of America"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.cambridge.org\/core\/services\/aop-cambridge-core\/content\/view\/S0424820100151118","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2020,6,18]],"date-time":"2020-06-18T10:30:43Z","timestamp":1592476243000},"score":53.640312,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.cambridge.org\/core\/product\/identifier\/S0424820100151118\/type\/journal_article"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[1993,8,1]]},"references-count":3,"alternative-id":["S0424820100151118"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/s0424820100151118","ISSN":["0424-8201","2690-1315"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0424-8201","type":"print"},{"value":"2690-1315","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[1993,8,1]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2022,4,2]],"date-time":"2022-04-02T13:00:37Z","timestamp":1648904437706},"reference-count":4,"publisher":"Cambridge University Press (CUP)","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2020,6,18]],"date-time":"2020-06-18T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1592438400000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":9076,"URL":"https:\/\/www.cambridge.org\/core\/terms"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Proc. annu. meet. Electron Microsc. Soc. Am."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1995,8,13]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Scanning tunneling microscopy (STM) can image clean and adsorbate-covered surfaces with atomic\/molecular resolution. This enables us to obtain detailed information on how catalytic reactions proceed on surfaces. Information on such topics as initiation sites for chemical reactions, reaction trends, the development of molecular order, and mesoscopic surface restructuring can be obtained. In addition, variable temperature STM experiments can yield insight into the decomposition of molecules at surfaces.<\/jats:p><jats:p>Studies using STM under ultra-high vaccuum conditions have shown how the oxidation of CO occurs on oxygen-precovered Rh(110) surfaces. Figure 1 shows an STM image of an oxygen-precovered Rh(110) surface displaying areas of oxygen-induced c(2\u00d76) and c(2\u00d78) reconstructions following exposure to 5 Langmuirs of CO. Images like this show that the reaction between the CO and adsorbed oxygen initiates at step edges and defects sites. The CO reaction fronts then proceed in a onedimensional manner stripping away the oxgyen from two and three atom wide islands.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1017\/s0424820100138488","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2020,6,18]],"date-time":"2020-06-18T09:51:31Z","timestamp":1592473891000},"page":"422-423","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Scanning tunneling microscopy studies of reactions at surfaces"],"prefix":"10.1017","volume":"53","author":[{"given":"F.M.","family":"Leibsle","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"56","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2020,6,18]]},"reference":[{"key":"S0424820100138488_ref03","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0039-6028(94)90340-9"},{"key":"S0424820100138488_ref01","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/363706a0"},{"key":"S0424820100138488_ref02","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevLett.72.2569"},{"key":"S0424820100138488_ref04","unstructured":"4. Leibsle, F. M. , Haq, S. , and Bowker, M. , (in preparation)."}],"container-title":["Proceedings, annual meeting, Electron Microscopy Society of America"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.cambridge.org\/core\/services\/aop-cambridge-core\/content\/view\/S0424820100138488","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2020,6,18]],"date-time":"2020-06-18T10:32:08Z","timestamp":1592476328000},"score":52.743145,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.cambridge.org\/core\/product\/identifier\/S0424820100138488\/type\/journal_article"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[1995,8,13]]},"references-count":4,"alternative-id":["S0424820100138488"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/s0424820100138488","ISSN":["0424-8201","2690-1315"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0424-8201","type":"print"},{"value":"2690-1315","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[1995,8,13]]}}],"items-per-page":5,"query":{"start-index":0,"search-terms":null}}}